From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jacob McSwain <jacob@mcswain.dev>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:17:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(gateway): a restart holds what it would refuse for the
 next gateway

gateway.restart_listener_hold_seconds (0 = off; needs restart_listener_handover and restart_listener_relay_seconds): from the stop signal to the profile release, a request or WebSocket upgrade the gateway would refuse with 503 gateway_not_ready (close 1013) waits up to that bound instead. Once the profile is released it is forwarded, as HTTP or as a WebSocket, to the gateway that took over, and so is every later request on a connection the old listener already had, until the relay window ends. With the key every GET is served while the stores are open, and a Webapp WebSocket opened before the restart wait stays open through it.
